FLOOD -- the timing of a network call.  Dial pulses on A, flooded, monitored and claimed.
  Arithmetic from measured constants, not a simulation of the gates:
    register windows HIT 8 / ID 128 ms (register.md 2); MT8870 StD 40 ms; A path per hop: a fall
    2.0 ms, a rise 1.5 ms (aline 1); a seizure crosses an exchange in 7 ms; marker action 2 ms;
    sender 20 pps 60/40 with 200 ms between digits (register.md 3 read 20 pps; mf8-cards.md 5 carried it);
    guard, seizure to first break, 200 ms; release 256 ms.  The caller starts dialling 1 s after dial tone.

  1. 2144 dials 2355 on 21 = 22 = 23 = 24.  A rotary caller; junctors seized when the FIRST digit is in.
